sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0248, Cluster router resolver amendment. Shared publication with Cluster-only DNS delegates and no automatic VPN fallback.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten rules 18, 22, 27, 28: one phase per target, parallel targets, shared peer policy, retain old paths until members confirm.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · shared DNS publication
  %% kind: dns.publish
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane M icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as DNS Nodes<br/>VPN · Routers
  participant M as LAN members<br/>includes Router
  Note over GW: Render DNS and selection<br/>one database revision
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads stored desired and pending Route, Cluster, Router and membership rows in the revision transaction
  %%> - builds the VPN WireGuard answers, Router LAN answers for its LAN members, and each member's Cluster delegate and remaining VPN policy from one address-selection rule
  %%> - includes explicit retirement targets from unfinished transitions; a missing row alone never authorizes deletion
  %%> - pre-cutover preparation sets cluster_only: it publishes Router projections and member policies through this same phase while leaving the VPN listener in place
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>child dns-publish
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - revision, target renders, member policies, expected answers and pinned SSH connections; no step fetches intent from the Gateway
  %%> - the owning command retains its lifecycle lock and receives this child's terminal result
  Note over SW: Write the intent
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes private run files and ships the existing Ansible assets once
  SW->>N: Publish resolver files<br/>dns-publish.yml · forEach
  %%> How:
  %%> - independent VPN and Router targets run in parallel; each target takes its DNS lock and validates, snapshots, installs and checks in one phase
  %%> - the Router's isolated unit binds its LAN address only and forwards unmatched names directly to VPN DNS; VPN DNS never forwards back
  %%> - reuse the templates, revision check, reload-on-change and local recovery; only unit, paths, bind set and upstream policy differ
  %%> Result:
  %%> - answers checked over UDP and TCP; A, AAAA NODATA, exact-name descendants and nested TLD exceptions match the target render
  alt revision already installed
    %% path: superseded
    Note over N: Skipped — superseded<br/>dns.revision_superseded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no write or reload; receipt names the actual revision and projection digest
    %%> - only matching effective projections authorize dependent member selection or retirement; an obsolete run cannot remove a newer resolver
  else newer revision
    %% path: newer-revision
    N-->>SW: Resolver receipts<br/>revision · digest · answers
    %%> Result:
    %%> - records the revision last, after checks; record-only changes use SIGHUP and unchanged content leaves the PID alone
    %%> - a changed startup configuration restarts only that resolver; the snapshot remains until the phase commits
  end
  SW->>M: Apply member DNS policy<br/>shared peer phase · forEach
  %%> When:
  %%> - only changed member policies, after their required resolver projections pass; the lifecycle caller waits for every affected member
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - first persists and activates VPN coverage for old and new private domains, then reloads the replacement delegate, then narrows VPN to its final scope; brief private overlap is allowed, including on withdrawal
  %%> - keeps owned exact domains beneath foreign VPN namespaces as more specific delegate exceptions; no equal suffix remains on both scopes at steady state
  %%> - checks uncached Cluster A, another private name, public resolution and the actual selected scope; the resolver publication checks AAAA NODATA
  %%> Unsupported members:
  %%> - systemd below 258 or missing delegate support keeps VPN selection; returns dns.cluster_delegate_unsupported and Doctor reports it
  %%> Runtime failure:
  %%> - Cluster resolver or LAN failure makes selected Cluster lookups fail until repair; Doctor reports it and no automatic VPN fallback runs
  opt replacing or withdrawing
    %% path: retire
    Note over SW: Wait the DNS grace<br/>one shared 31-second grace
    %%> Why:
    %%> - every affected member has confirmed its new policy before cached answers to the old address can expire
    %%> - persist the last successful DNS selection time; retries wait only the remaining grace, while any newer successful selection resets the deadline
    %%> - this shared barrier alone owns the wait; Route reconciliation and Router transitions consume it without another grace
    %%> - only a successfully persisted member receipt with no member failure passes; a prepared receipt followed by commit failure or rollback never authorizes retirement
    %%> - if any member fails or is offline, no retirement runs and the old resolver, sites and LAN rules remain
    SW->>N: Retire unused resolvers<br/>dns-publish.yml · absent
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes only the explicitly retired unit and fences its revision; retained configuration and recovery files do not authorize service activation
    %%> - the owning command can then retire the old Router sites and prune its LAN rules
  end
  Note over SW: Remove the run folder
  %%> How:
  %%> - native completed dependencies remove disposable intent and assets after work stops, including on failure
  %%> - public receipts come from the phases; no separate reporting or assertion script
  alt required phases pass
    %% path: succeeded
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the shared reader projects each applied revision and digest; the owner may finish its transition
  else publication or member fails
    %% path: failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed target · error_code
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a failed changed phase restores its own captured files and live policy; a failed restore retains its snapshot and reports dns.rollback_failed
    %%> - successful targets remain applied; the old Router and DNS stay reachable while any member still selects them
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - keep the unfinished transition and receipts; resume or render fresh stored state with a newer revision
    %%> - never replay an older whole-fleet snapshot over later changes; cleanup failure stays visible
  end
